# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This repo previously carried a mix (75 of 249 Python files were CRLF, the rest
# LF). Nothing read the difference -- Python's universal newlines make both
# identical at runtime -- but git stores bytes, so any tool that round-tripped a
# CRLF file through a text read/write silently rewrote every line and turned a
# small edit into a whole-file diff.
#
# `text=auto` lets git classify: files it detects as binary (NUL bytes) are left
# byte-exact. The explicit entries below cover formats where that heuristic
# should not be relied on.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.pdf     binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.xls     binary
*.zip     binary
